        "mission_intent": "Subject: SOX Compliance \u2013 Statute of Limitations and Sentencing Guidelines Policy Update\n\nTeam, we need a comprehensive update to our internal compliance and legal-risk framework to reflect the statute of limitations provisions under Section 804 of the Sarbanes-Oxley Act as well as the sentencing guideline review requirements under Section 805. Specifically, the policy document should codify that any private action involving a claim of fraud, deceit, manipulation, or contravention of the securities laws (as cross-referenced with Section 3(a)(47) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934) must account for a limitations period of two years from discovery of the violation or five years from the date of the violation, whichever is earlier. The document must clearly note that this limitations period applies only to proceedings commenced on or after the Act's enactment date of July 30, 2002, and must explicitly state that no new private right of action is created by these provisions. Additionally, include a section summarizing the Commission's obligation to review and amend Federal Sentencing Guidelines for obstruction of justice and extensive criminal fraud under Section 805 and how that impacts our risk exposure assessments. Please have this routed through Legal and the Audit Committee for review by end of next week.",
